OL,3,GNEWSAFirm fined over fatal fire
OL,4,Aextinguisher discharge
OL,5,
OL,6,FA waste and recycling company has been
OL,7,Ffined after a father of four was killed
OL,8,Fwhile working on a fire extinguisher as
OL,9,Fpart of his duties.
OL,11,FCraig Pearson, 37, from Dudley, was
OL,12,Fworking for Fire Protection Recycling
OL,13,FLimited at its site in Oldbury when the
OL,14,Fincident happened on 7 March 2023.
OL,16,FHe had been processing powder fire
OL,17,Fextinguishers which were at the end of
OL,18,Ftheir serviceable life. While working
OL,19,Fon a cartridge-type extinguisher, it
OL,20,Fhad a sudden release of pressure and
OL,21,Fexploded, striking him in the head.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
